  "body (notes 16, 17, 23): the two dots of qāf are printed merged into a short stroke in «قعح», «قمح», «قنب», «قيب», «قصو» and «قصب», those of yāʾ in «يه» and «قيب»; the «ى» (10) of note 16 is printed without dots.",
  "body (note 16): the t of the first «Pts.» is printed with a blot below it.",
